 * One tier above the strongest of these, frontier at most, premium included; a family no tier
146-Each agent runs on a model **family**: a tier (`economy`, `standard`, `frontier`) or a role
147-(`reviewer`, `researcher`, `implementer`, `planner`). `assign` in `skraft-config.json` (or in
148:`~/.skraft/config.json`, or an uncommitted `skraft-config.local.json`) picks each agent's family;
149-`models` says what a family runs on per host, with an effort. `skraft doctor` shows the
150-resolved assignment. How-to: [Choose the agents' models](https://sebastiendegodez.github.io/skraft-plugin/how-to/choose-models).
151-
152-## Supported stacks
153-
154-| Stack | Clean Architecture | Quality gates and mutation | Mocking and contract tests |
155-|---|---|---|---|
156-| .NET | `clean-architecture-dotnet` | `quality-gates-dotnet` (Stryker.NET) | Microcks (default) or in-process doubles; `WebApplicationFactory` |
157-| Python | `clean-architecture-python` | `quality-gates-python` (cosmic-ray) | Microcks (default) or respx; FastAPI `TestClient` |
158-| Java / Spring Boot | `clean-architecture-java` | not yet | not yet |
159-| TypeScript back end (Node, Vitest) | `clean-architecture-typescript` | `quality-gates-typescript` (StrykerJS on Vitest) | MSW (default) or Microcks |
160-| React / TypeScript (Vitest) | `clean-architecture-react` | `quality-gates-typescript` (StrykerJS on Vitest) | MSW (default) or Microcks; no contract test, a front end exposes no API |
161-| Node JavaScript | — | `quality-gates-javascript` (`node --test`, StrykerJS TAP) | MSW (default) or Microcks |
